{
  "description": "Sales-form money rule (U-122, sales-cents-v1) shared by the engine (packages/api/src/utils/sales-compute.ts: invoices and cash sales; credit memo lines use the line rule) and the ClientLedger client (fixtures/invoices/golden.json, byte-identical). Synthetic. Every amount is a decimal string; rates are fractions (\"0.081\" = 8.1 %).",
  "rules": {
    "lineAmount": "round2(quantity x unitPrice), half away from zero (decimal.js ROUND_HALF_UP, precision 40). quantity and unitPrice: decimal strings with at most 4 places; either may be negative.",
    "taxRate": "A line's taxRate when sent, else the request company's default rate; rounded half away from zero to the 4 places journal_lines.tax_rate stores; 0 <= rate < 1. A line that is not taxable has rate 0.",
    "tax": "Once per document and rate: round2(taxable base x rate), half away from zero. The taxable base is the SIGNED sum of the taxable line amounts at that rate, so a taxable negative line (a discount or a return) reduces it (Q-P20t). On a document whose subtotal is above 0.00, a rate's base never goes below 0.00 (Q-P20ag): a negative base taxes 0.00, every line of that rate gets tax 0.00, and the document taxableBase counts it as 0.00; the negative lines still lower the subtotal and the total. A document whose subtotal is 0.00 or less (a return) reverses its tax: its bases and tax stay negative (Q-P20aj). Different rates on one document are separate groups whose taxes add up.",
    "allocation": "Mixed-sign and discount rule: the group's tax is split over its taxable lines by largest remainder. Each line's exact share is amount x rate. In cents, every share is floored toward minus infinity (so -72.5 cents floors to -73), the remainders (each in [0, 1)) are kept, and the cents still missing to reach the rounded tax (a whole number from 0 to the line count) go one each to the lines with the largest remainder, the earlier line first on a tie. Line taxes therefore always sum exactly to the document tax, whatever the signs. Lines that are not taxable get 0.00.",
    "total": "subtotal (sum of line amounts) + tax total. Every figure is exact at 2 places; the ledger stores them at 4 (\"154.7200\")."
  },
