  "pricingRules": {
    "unitPrice": "Item kinds (U-39a, item-kinds-sales-v1): service, non_inventory, other_charge, discount, subtotal. For a line that is not a discount or subtotal: the line's unitPrice when sent (source input); else the client's price level fixed price for the item (price_level); else round2(item price x (1 + level percent / 100)) (price_level_percent); else the item's price (item); else 400 VALIDATION_ERROR. quantity omitted is 1. Then the U-122 line rule.",
    "priceLevel": "Price levels (U-40, price-levels-v1, Q-P20l): a name and a signed percent (-7.5 = 7.5 % down; -100 to 1000, at most 4 places) plus optional fixed prices for chosen items (stored rounded half away from zero to the cent); one level per client. A level price is round2(item price x (1 + percent / 100)), half away from zero. Discount and subtotal items never take a level price.",
    "discount": "A discount line (item kind discount) applies to its group: the signed sum of the line amounts since the last subtotal line (earlier discounts included); a discount right under a subtotal takes that subtotal's amount, and each discount right under that one takes the subtotal less the discounts between them (stacked discounts compound; later subtotals still show the lines since the previous subtotal); with nothing above it the group is 0.00. Percent (the line's discountPercent, else the item's; 0 < p <= 100): amount = -round2(group x p / 100), half away from zero, and 0.00 when the group is 0.00 or less (a discount never adds). Amount (the line's unitPrice, else the item's price): amount = -|round2(price)|. quantity is not used; sending both discountPercent and unitPrice is 400. Discount items are taxable unless set otherwise: a taxable discount is a negative taxable line and reduces the taxable base (Q-P20t); a non-taxable discount leaves the base whole.",
    "subtotal": "A subtotal line (item kind subtotal) shows the signed sum of the line amounts since the previous subtotal. It is not part of the document subtotal, the taxable base or the total and is never taxed; quantity and unitPrice are ignored. It posts as a $0 line.",
    "preview": "POST /invoices/preview computes with the same code as POST and PUT /invoices (packages/api/src/utils/invoice-compute.ts) and posts nothing: for the same body its lines and totals equal what the invoice posts."
  },
  "pricingCases": [
