  "billableRules": {
    "cost": "costAmount = round2(the source line's debit - credit), half away from zero, sign kept (a 4-place bill or check cost becomes cents here, so A/R stays cent-exact).",
    "markup": "markupPercent is a percent (\"10\" = 10 %), 0 to 1000, at most 4 places. markupAmount = round2(costAmount x markupPercent / 100), half away from zero. A negative cost takes no markup and passes through at cost (Q-P20z): its effective markupPercent is 0.",
    "line": "One visible line (Q-P20w): amount = costAmount + markupAmount; quantity = the source quantity, else 1; the rate shown (unitPrice, unitPriceSource billable_cost) = round4(amount / quantity). Price levels never reprice it; a discount after it covers its full amount, markup included. Tax is computed on the visible amount (the U-122 rule).",
    "journal": "The cost line credits the line's own income account for costAmount and carries the line's taxAmount; the markup line (only when markupAmount is not 0) credits the company markup account for markupAmount with taxAmount 0. Both carry billableSourceLineId; lineRole billable_cost / billable_markup."
  },
  "billableCases": [
